{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/373394-losts-population-explosion","id":373394,"title":"Losts population explosion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-17T01:20:50-08:00","id":373394,"title":"Losts population explosion","content":"As most of you know, I run an episodic game for our RPG club about creation of changelings Freehold in small ( about 2500 citizens ), town in New England. As there are surprisingly high population of Lost in there ( now it's something like about 10 changelings returning in few weeks, and still counting ) it's one of main &quot;meta-mysteries&quot; of the game and glue of the game. Second is sudden disappearance of previous, first colonization Freehold a 200-300 years ago.<br /> <br /> But here is a thing - I got the problem ( there are many people missing and returning in this place ) but still do not have answer on it, or even ideas on possible answers. Question of topic is simple: <b>What could be reason for this high ( almost tidal ) return of Lost to this very much location, in such high numbers?</b> Suddenly, they will be like 1% of population in general citizens in short notice.<br /> <br /> On first though I got idea it's some kind of Gentry play, where Lords and Ladies are letting changelings free for they own amusement - but I still do not have <i>why</i> would they done this. <b>Why would couple of Keepers steal many humans in region for years, and suddenly now let them free in almost the same time?</b><br /> <br /> Or maybe you have a better reason than this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-17-2015, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T02:05:45-08:00","id":373431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/373394-losts-population-explosion#post373394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As most of you know, I run an episodic game for our RPG club about creation of changelings Freehold in small ( about 2500 citizens ), town in New England. As there are surprisingly high population of Lost in there ( now it's something like about 10 changelings returning in few weeks, and still counting ) it's one of main &quot;meta-mysteries&quot; of the game and glue of the game. Second is sudden disappearance of previous, first colonization Freehold a 200-300 years ago.<br /> <br /> But here is a thing - I got the problem ( there are many people missing and returning in this place ) but still do not have answer on it, or even ideas on possible answers. Question of topic is simple: <b>What could be reason for this high ( almost tidal ) return of Lost to this very much location, in such high numbers?</b> Suddenly, they will be like 1% of population in general citizens in short notice.<br /> <br /> On first though I got idea it's some kind of Gentry play, where Lords and Ladies are letting changelings free for they own amusement - but I still do not have <i>why</i> would they done this. <b>Why would couple of Keepers steal many humans in region for years, and suddenly now let them free in almost the same time?</b><br /> <br /> Or maybe you have a better reason than this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Someone recently recreate a landmark that had been demolished years ago. It becomes an anchor in the minds of many of the refugees and helps guide them home.<br /> <br /> 2. A Pledge was struck here a long time ago with a Lady. Wrestled from her from an iron spear. All Lost that encountered her in the hedge would be herded out the Hedge to the town's Trods. To the Freehold's dismay, she thoroughly enjoys the challenge of the badly worded Pledge, both nipping at the heels of recently escaped changelings to the town and keeping the town's changelings out of the Hedge.<br /> <br /> 3. A True Fae died. Not diminished of lost title but gambled it's very Name and lost. It's former slaves are making a break for it and it just so happens that the town is the closest trod that they can escape to.<br /> <br /> 4. All of the above.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T10:30:19-08:00","id":373605,"title":"","content":"Bravo, Shock! I especially like option 3 -- it sets up a sprawling meta-plot involving the struggle for the Title.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T11:03:30-08:00","id":373619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/373394-losts-population-explosion#post373394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Why would couple of Keepers steal many humans in region for years, and suddenly now let them free in almost the same time?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>For fun.<br /> <br /> To imagine the mentality of solipsistic God-monsters with little understanding of human emotion, the easy go-to perspective is that everything is a game. A game with horrifying consequences for everybody else involved.<br /> <br /> So the reason for this &quot;catch and release&quot; policy could be the setup for a competitive hunt for the Gentry. Think of how most fox hunts work: the fox has already been captured, days in advance. The fox is released purely so that the spectacle and thrill of horns and hounds baying can have a target. The Gentry care about the Hunt more than the Prey.<br /> <br /> A group of True Fae start dribbling changelings into a local area. Arcane rules are set in place. Once the freehold population reached a saturated point, the trigger fires. It's all-you-can-abduct, kill-what-you-want Fae Freehold-for-all. If they drag back more souls than they previously released, good for them: they possibly won the game.<br /> <br /> That can be what happened oh so many years ago, with the previous population. In one frantic evening, everyone Lost or near them was thrown into a sack or torn apart by ice-hounds. And it's going to happen again.<br /> <br /> If the motley discover this, how can they stop it? Maybe spreading the new arrivals out into distant freeholds will dissipate the focus of the hunters. Perhaps the nature of the game requires some very specific conditions which can be spoiled before it even starts. Maybe the only thing to do is try to shore up the trods, load up with iron arms and pray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T11:07:20-08:00","id":373621,"title":"","content":"In my changeling game there was a True Fae we, thankfully, didn't encounter who was known to take entire villages and towns of people.<br /> <br /> If something like that died or lost their Title or was exiled, their changelings would be free.<br /> <br /> However, the only changeling we met from it was essentially a loyalist, so it's possible they're releasing 'regular' changelings en masse to let infiltrators into established freeholds, ready to throw the doors wide when their new master comes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T11:30:28-08:00","id":373637,"title":"","content":"<b>Notice:</b> PCs changes from game to game, because - as I mentioned - it's episodic game of &quot;one session per few weeks&quot;. I let various players in the game choose various Keepers, so they would not suspect &quot;it's an Arcadian Huntsman trick!&quot; plot. So on the plate we have return of many changelings from at least few diffrent Keepers, not only one True Fae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/373394-losts-population-explosion?p=373619#post373619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the reason for this &quot;catch and release&quot; policy could be the setup for a competitive hunt for the Gentry. Think of how most fox hunts work: the fox has already been captured, days in advance. The fox is released purely so that the spectacle and thrill of horns and hounds baying can have a target. The Gentry care about the Hunt more than the Prey.<br /> <br /> A group of True Fae start dribbling changelings into a local area. Arcane rules are set in place. Once the freehold population reached a saturated point, the trigger fires. It's all-you-can-abduct, kill-what-you-want Fae Freehold-for-all. If they drag back more souls than they previously released, good for them: they possibly won the game.<br /> <br /> That can be what happened oh so many years ago, with the previous population. In one frantic evening, everyone Lost or near them was thrown into a sack or torn apart by ice-hounds. And it's going to happen again.<br /> <br /> If the motley discover this, how can they stop it? Maybe spreading the new arrivals out into distant freeholds will dissipate the focus of the hunters. Perhaps the nature of the game requires some very specific conditions which can be spoiled before it even starts. Maybe the only thing to do is try to shore up the trods, load up with iron arms and pray.</div> </div> </div> </div>I come to think about something like this, you know. When reading <b>Equinox Road</b> I recalled something called Feud - with is &quot;alliance&quot; of compiting True Fae. They drive each other stories and Titles as rivals, so it's a everlasing tradition to have ceremonial enemies. I think that local Feud could put they all belongings ( Titles ) and opened <i>the Game</i> to commerce - &quot;let all the Lost on they way to this little town, and let them build Courts and Freehold. The one that get's the most back after a year of time, will win all the prizes&quot; - is that sound as enough True Fae plan?<br /> <br /> Secondary questions: <b>How this kind of deal coud be broken? How could PCs get to know this plan? Would True Fae send Loyalists?</b><br /> <br /> I plan to run a game about a session in this chronicle about masquared ball, on what some fae being would summon PCs. Maybe I will make a host of Charlatean that was a part of Feud and now it;s trying to get revange for sending him from Arcadia on the Feud? And to this he wants to use PCs and changeling in area? Clearly, if I would go with that, Charlatean would come to be a murderer killing his guest to &quot;give them a massage&quot;, but - still - he would try to help PCs. Somehow....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T12:59:09-08:00","id":373700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/373394-losts-population-explosion?p=373637#post373637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I come to think about something like this, you know. When reading <b>Equinox Road</b> I recalled something called Feud - with is &quot;alliance&quot; of compiting True Fae. They drive each other stories and Titles as rivals, so it's a everlasing tradition to have ceremonial enemies. I think that local Feud could put they all belongings ( Titles ) and opened <i>the Game</i> to commerce - &quot;let all the Lost on they way to this little town, and let them build Courts and Freehold. The one that get's the most back after a year of time, will win all the prizes&quot; - is that sound as enough True Fae plan? </div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much exactly what I had in my head. It's a good idea to have it worded in the way of a contract between the Fae, too. I'll get to that in a bit...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/373394-losts-population-explosion?p=373637#post373637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondary questions: <b>How this kind of deal coud be broken? How could PCs get to know this plan? Would True Fae Send Loyalists? </b></div> </div> </div> </div>Loyalists? Absolutely. The Gentry are just like real English gentry: they employ a mob of workers to ensure the hunt goes the way they wish. Beaters, houndsmen, groundskeepers... all they do is ensure that the stage is set for the Master's slaughter.<br /> <br /> They could find out about it in a few different ways. Suspicions could start with small observations: dreams of portent, an eerie silence in the Hedge, any number of strange resonances in the Wyrd. Final confirmation could come from a captured Loyalist or a local prophet/seer. Maybe a rare written record from the last time this happened is found. I love the idea of Banished Fae: you don't even need to give them too much of a sensible motive. They tend to be absolutely insane, even for the Gentry, so you can have one babbling about &quot;what's coming&quot; as he/she paces around a derelict building or muttering about having &quot;lost&quot; while slumped in an alleyway.<br /> <br /> Breaking the deal is where the exact wording of the contract can come into play. Throw ideas around, the more arcane the better. Perhaps the whole thing kicks off &quot;When the First Summer Sunrise graces the Haert of the Townstead.&quot; Turns out, all you need to do is cover up the statue of a stag in the middle of town with some heavy blankets, holding the whole thing off indefinitely. Any number of events could be essential precursors to the Hunt. True Fae are literally incapable of deviating from such clauses. If the players can find out the exact words of the agreement, they're halfway to saving everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4722,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","user":"Birnam","date":". 01-17-2015, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T16:15:52-08:00","id":373910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/373394-losts-population-explosion#post373394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What could be reason for this high ( almost tidal ) return of Lost to this very location, in such high numbers?</b><br /> <br /> <b>Why would couple of Keepers steal many humans in region for years, and suddenly now let them free in almost the same time?</b></div> </div> </div> </div> You already seem to have decided, so forgive the intrusion. My idea is that they realeced them out of spite. Not the Changelings; another Gentry. One that doesn't play by the rules, one who doesn't plan to conflict, but to win. Maybe he's a general who just wants to kill his Peers; maybe it's a &quot;Therapist&quot;, one who's started believing his own role and that the other Kindly Ones are the mad ones, and need to be locked away &quot;for their own good&quot;(if you go with this one, maybe highlight how their &quot;treatment&quot; parallels the Durance)Either way, he's capturing or killing all the Fae, while completely ignoring Changelings(making it trivially easy to escape)... For now. You see, with each Keeper he kills/enslaves, he absorbs their component parts and link to the Wyrd. If not stopped, he'll win; and all that will be left for this monster, a being akin to deities compared to beings akin to deities, will be Ironside.<br /> Basically, the Changelings may have to save their Keepers to save the world. Sorry for interrupting with such a stupid idea.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As to why here, it's because a Fae Banished itself to survive(obviously a last-ditch effort), and in the process marked a &quot;route&quot; that Changelings unconsciously follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Fixes stuff 01-17-2015, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}